        "is_free": true,
        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Project Cottontails</strong> is a short interactive story set inside the Civic Museum of Manduria. You play as Alessio, a thoughtful young man exploring a faithfully recreated 3D version of the museum, where forgotten fragments of his grandfather’s past — a former Allied pilot in World War II — begin to surface.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This isn’t a gameplay-heavy title, nor a long adventure packed with challenges. It’s something smaller, more personal. A first step in blending technology, storytelling, and historical memory. It lasts about twenty minutes — just enough, we hope, to leave a quiet impression. The story is simple and subdued, designed to stir emotion without relying on spectacle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One of the core goals of the project is to <strong>preserve and share a real cultural site</strong>, offering virtual access to a piece of history that many might never be able to visit in person. In this sense, <i>Project Cottontails</i> is also an experiment in digital preservation — a way to open the doors of local heritage to a wider world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is just the beginning. The project is intentionally minimal, but built with the idea of growing over time — with new content, deeper historical layers, and new places to explore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you decide to take this short journey, thank you. We hope it leaves you with something — and maybe, in time, it can become something more.</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Project Cottontails</strong> is a short interactive story set inside the Civic Museum of Manduria. You play as Alessio, a thoughtful young man exploring a faithfully recreated 3D version of the museum, where forgotten fragments of his grandfather’s past — a former Allied pilot in World War II — begin to surface.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This isn’t a gameplay-heavy title, nor a long adventure packed with challenges. It’s something smaller, more personal. A first step in blending technology, storytelling, and historical memory. It lasts about twenty minutes — just enough, we hope, to leave a quiet impression. The story is simple and subdued, designed to stir emotion without relying on spectacle.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >One of the core goals of the project is to <strong>preserve and share a real cultural site</strong>, offering virtual access to a piece of history that many might never be able to visit in person. In this sense, <i>Project Cottontails</i> is also an experiment in digital preservation — a way to open the doors of local heritage to a wider world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is just the beginning. The project is intentionally minimal, but built with the idea of growing over time — with new content, deeper historical layers, and new places to explore.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you decide to take this short journey, thank you. We hope it leaves you with something — and maybe, in time, it can become something more.</p>",
        "short_description": "&quot;Project Cottontails&quot; is an interactive narrative adventure in the Manduria Civic Museum. Step into the shoes of Alessio, explore the museum, interact with characters and objects to piece together the story of your ancestor, a famous Allied aviator in World War II.",
